AI Training Rider

This rider is an additional condition on the permission granted above. It
narrows the MIT grant; where the two conflict, this rider governs. Because of
it, this license is not the unmodified MIT license and is not an OSI-approved
open source license.

1. Reserved use. No permission is granted to use the Software, in whole or in
   part, as input to the training, pre-training, fine-tuning, distillation,
   reinforcement learning, retrieval-augmented indexing, evaluation-set
   construction, or other development of any machine learning model, language
   model, or generative artificial intelligence system, nor to include it in
   any corpus or dataset assembled for those purposes. This applies whether
   the resulting model is published, sold, or kept internal.

2. Automated collection. Scraping, crawling, mirroring, or bulk-downloading
   the Software for the purposes in section 1 is likewise not permitted. A
   robots.txt, terms of service, or licence metadata on any host that
   distributes the Software does not enlarge this grant.

3. Permitted uses. This rider does not restrict any other use allowed by the
   MIT terms above. In particular it does not restrict reading, running,
   modifying, or redistributing the Software; using an AI assistant to help
   you write, review, or explain code in a project that depends on the
   Software; or a model processing the Software transiently at inference time
   without retaining it as training data.

4. Separate permission. Rights withheld by this rider may be granted in
   writing by the copyright holder. Absent that writing, they are reserved.

5. Severability. If any part of this rider is held unenforceable, the
   remainder stays in force, and the MIT terms above continue to apply to
   everything the rider does not reach.

